rary About Library Facilities and Services Rules and regulations Library OPAC UGC e-Resources Indian History, Culture and Society Link Gallery E News Letter Facilities & Others Hostel Boy’s Hostel Girl’s Hostel Canteen Sports Transport Certificate Courses College Committee List Best Practices Grievance Anti-ragging & Anti Sexual Harassment cell Youth Red Cross Cell SC-ST/OBC CELL Student Feedback Links Calendar Of Events 2025-26 VTU Syllabus VTU EXAM TIME TABLE Multilingual Books Alumni Cell NSDC Contact us About us Management Director Office Principal Academics Courses Research (Ph.D) Undergraduate Programmes (B.E.) Departments Applied Science and Humanities Computer Science Engineering Electronics and Communication Engineering Mechanical Engineering Robotics and Artificial Intelligence Placement cell Multilingual Library About Library Facilities and Services Rules and regulations Library OPAC UGC e-Resources Indian History, Culture and Society Link Gallery E News Letter Facilities & Others Hostel Boy’s Hostel Girl’s Hostel Canteen Sports Transport Certificate Courses College Committee List Best Practices Grievance Anti-ragging & Anti Sexual Harassment cell Youth Red Cross Cell SC-ST/OBC CELL Student Feedback Links Calendar Of Events 2025-26 VTU Syllabus VTU EXAM TIME TABLE Multilingual Books Alumni Cell NSDC Contact us WELCOME TO MMEC Late Mr. Nathajirao Halgekar Dr. Rajshree Nagaraju About MMEC Maratha Mandal Engineering College started functioning on the 21st of October 1997. The college has been duly sanctioned by the Government of Karnataka vide GO No. ED 32 UK 97′. Maratha Mandal Engineering College is recognized by the All India Council of Technical Education (AICTE), New Delhi vie letter no. F/77-153/220/(E)/ET/96 dated 4th August 1997. The College is affiliated to Visvesvaraya Technological University (VTU), Belgaum. The Institute is committed to generating, disseminating, and preserving knowledge, and to working with others to bring this knowledge to bear on the world’s great challenges. MMEC is dedicated to provide its students with an education that combines rigorous academic study and the excitement of discovery with the support and intellectual stimulation of a diverse campus community. We seek to develop in each learner of the MMEC the ability and passion to work wisely, creatively, and effectively for the betterment of the planet. Read more…. ADMISSION ENQUIRY NOTIFICATION The department of Electronics and Communication Engineering of Maratha Mandal's Engineering College Belagavi organised the Robo Race 2025. Robo Race 2025 where innovation is measured in milliseconds.!! on 06.11.2025 through staff and students association. Congratulation to Mr. Adityaraj for securing 3rd place in Karate Mr Adityaraj of 7th sem Compurer Science of Maratha Mandal Engineering College,Belagavi Visit to Industry by Mechanical Engineering Department Today students of 3rd semester Mechanical Engineering, MMEC visited Maruti Metals Pvt Ltd and Omkar Metals, Udyambag, Belagavi, a prominent manufacturer of cast iron components. Karnataka Rajyotsava Award presented to Dr.Rajshree Nagaraju, President, Maratha Mandal, Belagavi on 1st November at Bangalore. A long pending recognition for her women service in the field of education. CONGRATULATIONS Celebration of 70 th Karnataka Rajyotsava day AT MMEC on 1st November 2025. Wishing you all a joyful Karnataka Rajyotsava! FORESIGHTS AIM MISSION Our aim is to ensure that our students emerge as winners intellectually, ethically and professionally in future. We have some of the finest and most sincere minds working for us. Dedication, sincerity and continuing empathy of our teaching force get intellectually and emotionally translated into increased success of our students and satisfaction to all parents. To provide high quality education to acquaint with state of art technology. To adopt best practices to cope with industry standards and technological advancements. To inculcate personality traits to excel in communication and leadership skills with ethical and moral values. To strengthen bonds with industries, alumni and stakeholders through frequent interactions. VISION To emerge as leading engineering institute to impart excellent technical education and research opportunities to produce global leaders having professional skills in science and technology, managerial skills with socio-ethical values to cater the needs of the industries and nation ACHIEVEMENTS WORLD RECORD FOR SINGING Maratha Mandal Group of Institutes, Belagavi, Karnataka, India organised an event on the Republic day 26th January 2016, Where 15,000 participants uniformly dressed sung 5 patriotic songs simultaneously. The event was held at Maratha Mandal Engineering college Belagavi, Karnataka. Indian Book Of Records Maratha Mandal Group of Institutes, Belagavi, Karnataka, India organised an event on the Republic day 26th January 2016, Where 15,000 praticipants uniformly dressed sung 5 patriotic songs simultaneously. WORLD RECORD FOR DANCING Maratha Mandal Group of Institutes, Belagavi, Karnataka, India organised an event on The largest bollywood dance was achieved by Maratha mandal group of institutes, Belagavi, Karnataka, India on 5th February 2017 and have got the World Record for Dancing Undergraduate Programs Mechanical Engineering Robotics and AI Electronics and communication Computer Science GALLERY Poster Presentation(19/5/23) Poster Presentation(19/5/23) Ambedkar Jayanti @MMEC(14/4/2023) Ambedkar Jayanti @MMEC(14/4/2023) Sanitory pads were distributed in Ashte village on Women’s Day(8/3/23) MOU signed between 3Thub and MMEC(17/2/23) MOU signed between 3Thub and MMEC(17/2/23) INTERACT – A flagship program of 3Thub LLC(17/2/23) INTERACT – A flagship program of 3Thub LLC(17/2/23) INTERACT – A flagship program of 3Thub LLC(17/2/23) Skill Development Activity(2/2/2023) MICROSOFT INNOVATIVE EDUCATOR certificate Workshop on Analog & Digital Circuit Simulation using Cadence Tool(31/12/2022